  "observations": "Both current complete nine-component group views personally inspected. North-up view shows the principal northwest/southeast ridge sequence, uneven main mound with adjoining banks/southeastern platform, southwestern terrace and two lower Chaya-no-dan steps. Original hill and source grade remain visible between bounded component estimates; small edge gaps/overlaps are disclosed rather than hidden with filled terrain or a property-wide slab. Existing individual approvals are bound without reauthored geometry or extra individual captures. No medieval keep, invented clear moat, shrine proxy or standing stone wall added. Original field/frame/datum/ground sections remain unchanged.",
  "coverage": {
    "independentCurrentEarthworkConstituents": 9,
    "boundedScopeMembershipRecords": 9,
    "remainingLocalNativeFeatures": [],
    "scope": "Approximate present surviving Chihaya Castle earthwork ensemble: four principal enclosure grounds, southeastern enclosure, southwestern terrace, two current Chaya-no-dan outwork steps and narrow main-bailey northwest/west/south banks. Original current terrain shape and slope breaks retained. All nine bounded ground perimeters except the native lower-context ring are explicit authoring estimates; no archaeological survey, exact medieval edge/date or original grade is asserted. This is current ground form, not a restored medieval castle. Modern shrine/office/pavilion/Zondokan buildings, steles/signs/trees and undetectable lost ditch reconstructions are separate context; the whole natural hill is review terrain, not a castle solid.",
    "exactArchaeologicalPerimetersMeasured": false
  },
